# Files Cline should not read.
#
# Context is the scarcest resource in a session, and every one of these is either
# generated, enormous, or both. Reading them costs a large share of the window
# and teaches nothing about the codebase — build output in particular actively
# misleads, because it is a stale snapshot of source that has since changed.
#
# This is a READ filter, not a write ban. Cline can still be asked to change a
# lockfile deliberately; it just will not pull one in while exploring. Lockfiles
# matter here — #214 had to ship a follow-up commit for a widget lockfile that
# was missed — so if you add a dependency, update the lockfile on purpose.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
widget/node_modules/

# Build output
out/
dist/
dist-electron/
widget/dist/
widget/out/
widget/build/

# Test and report artifacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
widget/playwright-report/
widget/test-results/
coverage/

# Lockfiles — thousands of lines, no signal while exploring
package-lock.json
widget/package-lock.json

# Generated and append-only records
CHANGELOG.md
logs/
*.log

# Local state and binaries
memory/database/
memory/cache/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*

# Media fixtures and binaries
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.wav
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.ico
*.onnx
